  "bodyTypst": "Let $f$ be a function that has derivatives of all orders for all real numbers. Assume $f(0)= 5$, $f'(0)= - 3 \\, f''(0)= 1$, and $f'''(0)= 4$.\n\n(a) Write the third-degree Taylor polynomial for $f$ about $x = 0$ and use it to approximate $f(0.2)$.\n\n(b) Write the fourth-degree Taylor polynomial for $g$, where $g(x)= f lr((x^(2)))$, about $x = 0$.\n\n(c) Write the third-degree Taylor polynomial for $h$, where $h(x)= integral_(0)^(x) f(t) d t$, about $x = 0$.\n\n(d) Let $h$ be defined as in part (c). Given that $f(1)= 3$, either find the exact value of $h(1)$ or explain why it cannot be determined.",
